#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275495 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "feeec65c-f199-549e-808b-af504a539680" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275497} {:answer/id #uuid "04d7531a-3dd9-52fd-985a-3fd86ed94c0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{8}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275498} {:answer/id #uuid "098b131c-f332-585a-ac9c-fc691451a7b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275499} {:answer/id #uuid "ee51484c-a6a4-5f40-ac70-b492972d1b91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{6}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275500} {:answer/id #uuid "b7eb24a9-f854-5eb4-b75c-5d018fc4d870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7eb24a9-f854-5eb4-b75c-5d018fc4d870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275501} :answer-field/id #uuid "3753699b-067a-5d56-8d77-f4bf7a64563d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275496}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "185f98a1-a00c-5fde-987b-3fdb1c0ac8f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-72252" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971771/assets/28079ead5ebb4649900653172d11c25f3ff489c6b34772094a1ba947c18ef3e1.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-2,-2),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=3,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-2))^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
